course: dictionary
lesson: 11072
title: Weirdly: strange or surprising
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Weirdly is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens or how someone is. It means in a strange or unusual way. «Leo's sister noticed the mouth moved weirdly: it was a fake made by a computer.» A real mouth does not move like that, so weirdly means strangely.
explain: Weirdly can also come at the start of a sentence, where it means "strangely enough". It shows that something is surprising. «She's embarrassed, and also weirdly relieved she's not the only one.» Here weirdly tells you that the relief is a surprise.
explain: Use context to check your meaning. «Iona is weirdly proud.» Swap in strangely: Iona is strangely proud. It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Weirdly is an adverb: it tells you how something happens or how someone is.
fact: Weirdly means in a strange or unusual way.
fact: At the start of a sentence, weirdly means "strangely enough", to show that something is surprising.
fact: Everyday phrases include weirdly enough, weirdly quiet and acting weirdly.
exercise: «The mouth moved weirdly on the screen.» What does weirdly mean here? | In a very kind way | *In a strange or unusual way | Very loudly | In a quick and happy way
exercise: «Weirdly enough, the cat sat in the empty box.» What does weirdly enough show? | That the box is full | That it is raining | That the cat is sleepy | *That something is surprising
exercise: «Iona is weirdly proud.» Which word could replace weirdly without changing the meaning? | Loudly | Quickly | *Strangely | Gently
test: Ella says, «The room was weirdly quiet.» What does weirdly mean? | Very bright | Full of people | *Quiet in a strange way | Tidy and neat
test: Which sentence uses weirdly to show surprise? | The bus is big and blue | She ran to the bus stop | *Weirdly enough, the bus came early | Leo bought a ticket
exam: Jayden reads, «Weirdly, she's embarrassed and relieved.» Which meaning fits best? | *Strangely enough, she feels embarrassed and relieved | Weirdly means dangerous | The sky is grey and wet | She is very hungry
